<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Fitzwilliam Owen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1774–1857</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Fitzwilliam Owen was a British naval officer and hydrographer who surveyed much of the coast of East and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> in the 1820s. At Mombasa in 1824 he accepted the Mazrui rulers' request for protection against the Busaidi of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> and declared a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> on his own authority, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> disowned it and it ended in 1826.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-fitzwilliam-owen.jpg" alt="William Fitzwilliam Owen" width="320" height="448" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_Fitzwilliam_Owen.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
